# Code ownership → review routing. GitHub requests review from the owner automatically on any PR that
# touches a matching path. This is a small, single-maintainer project, so the default owner is the
# maintainer; the point of the specific rules below is to make the SAFETY-CRITICAL and CONTRACT paths
# impossible to change without that being visible in the review, not to distribute ownership.

# Default owner for everything.
*                                   @zgranowitz

# The cross-app contract mirror. faBolus's schema/command.schema.json is the source of truth; the
# Monkey C mirror lives in these files, and schema/remote-keys.txt + scripts/check-schema-drift.sh
# enforce that they don't drift. The check enforces the mirror; the semantics are a human concern.
/schema/                            @zgranowitz
/source/app/RemoteComm.mc           @zgranowitz
/source/app/AppState.mc             @zgranowitz

# The bolus-confirm interlock: the deliberate 1-2-3 tap (touch) and two-button hold (button). Never
# weaken these — the watch gesture is a second factor on top of the host's clamp (CONTRIBUTING.md).
/source/app/HoldView.mc             @zgranowitz
/source/app/HoldDelegate.mc         @zgranowitz
/source/app/BolusView.mc            @zgranowitz
/source/app/BolusDelegate.mc        @zgranowitz

# The most safety-critical code: the paused direct-to-pump engine signs and sends real pump commands
# and must stay byte-exact vs the pumpX2 oracle. It is excluded from every shipping build (P0-c) — keep
# any change to that exclusion visible.
/direct-pump/                       @zgranowitz

# CI, the branch model, governance, and licensing — changes to how the project proves and attributes
# itself.
/.github/                           @zgranowitz
/BRANCHES.md                        @zgranowitz
/CONTRIBUTING.md                    @zgranowitz
/AGENTS.md                          @zgranowitz
/NOTICE.md                          @zgranowitz
/THIRD_PARTY.md                     @zgranowitz
/docs/SBOM.md                       @zgranowitz
